# WAN-SQM cookbook validation fixture (#1828 Option C).
#
# The docs/cos-wan-sqm.md one-knob recipe: a BARE shaping-rate on the
# loss-userspace-cluster WAN unit (reth0 unit 80 -> the reth0.80 /
# 172.16.80.0/24 smoke path). No forwarding-classes, schedulers, or
# scheduler-maps on purpose — admission into CoS and the synthetic
# default best-effort queue come from the shaping-rate alone
# (contributes_usable_cos_state gate + synthetic queue_id 0 in
# userspace-dp/src/afxdp/forwarding_build/cos.rs), and per-flow MQFQ
# engages via lazy promotion when a second distinct flow contends
# (maybe_promote_best_effort in cos/queue_ops/push.rs, #1735).
#
# Rate: 3g (not the cookbook's 450m WAN example) so shaped vs unshaped
# is unambiguous against the ~23 Gbit/s lab line rate while the run
# stays quick. The mechanics under test are rate-independent.
#
# Pinned smoke assertions (full runnable snippet in docs/cos-wan-sqm.md
# "Validation recipe"):
#   (a) iperf3 -P 8 to 172.16.80.200 holds ~3 Gbit/s aggregate
#       (-P 8 not -P 2: promotion needs two flows on the SAME worker
#       queue; 8 flows over the WAN VF's 6 RSS queues pigeonhole one
#       worker into >=2 — see the doc's validation recipe);
#   (b) during/right after the run, at least one
#       xpf_userspace_cos_active_flow_count sample is > 1
#       (curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/metrics |
#        grep '^xpf_userspace_cos_active_flow_count' | awk '$2 > 1'
#        is non-empty) = MQFQ lazy promotion engaged;
#   (c) delete class-of-service + commit restores unshaped line rate.
#
# Compile guard: pkg/config/sqm_cookbook_fixture_test.go parses the
# `set` lines below on the production flat-set path and pins the
# compiled shaping rate, no scheduler-map, and no compile warnings.
#
# The delete line keeps the fixture idempotent when loaded as one
# atomic candidate (same convention as cos-iperf-config.set; scripts
# that inject their own delete list strip non-`set` lines).
delete class-of-service

set class-of-service interfaces reth0 unit 80 shaping-rate 3g
